Vulkan: samplerLodBiasMax is 0 where the portability subset forbids a mip LOD bias.

VK_KHR_portability_subset has a feature, samplerMipLodBias, without which every sampler must
have mipLodBias == 0 (VUID-VkSamplerCreateInfo-samplerMipLodBias-04467). MoltenVK on the GitHub
macOS runner ("Apple Paravirtual device", MoltenVK 1.4.2) reports the feature as false while
VkPhysicalDeviceLimits::maxSamplerLodBias stays non-zero, and NRI copies the limit into
DeviceDesc::other.samplerLodBiasMax. A caller that honours the reported limit therefore creates
a sampler the Khronos validation layer rejects (docs/findings.md 9).

NRI already chains VkPhysicalDevicePortabilitySubsetFeaturesKHR under __APPLE__ and reads
imageView2DOn3DImage from it; this reads samplerMipLodBias next to it and reports a limit of 0
when the feature is absent. No other platform is affected.

Applies on top of NRI v190 with patches 0001 to 0005.

diff --git a/Source/VK/DeviceVK.hpp b/Source/VK/DeviceVK.hpp
index cc92d62..0bf9234 100644
--- a/Source/VK/DeviceVK.hpp
+++ b/Source/VK/DeviceVK.hpp
@@ -1542,6 +1542,12 @@ Result DeviceVK::Create(const DeviceCreationDesc& desc, const DeviceCreationVKDe
         m_Desc.other.timestampFrequencyHz = uint64_t(1e9 / double(limits.timestampPeriod) + 0.5);
         m_Desc.other.drawIndirectMaxNum = limits.maxDrawIndirectCount;
         m_Desc.other.samplerLodBiasMax = limits.maxSamplerLodBias;
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+        // A portability device can forbid any non-zero "mipLodBias" ("samplerMipLodBias", "VUID-VkSamplerCreateInfo-samplerMipLodBias-04467")
+        // while its "maxSamplerLodBias" limit stays non-zero (MoltenVK). The limit reported here is the bias a sampler may actually use
+        if (IsExtensionSupported(VK_KHR_PORTABILITY_SUBSET_EXTENSION_NAME, desiredDeviceExts) && !PortabilitySubsetFeatures.samplerMipLodBias)
+            m_Desc.other.samplerLodBiasMax = 0.0f;
+#endif
         m_Desc.other.samplerAnisotropyMax = limits.maxSamplerAnisotropy;
         m_Desc.other.texelOffsetMin = (int8_t)limits.minTexelOffset;
         m_Desc.other.texelOffsetMax = (uint8_t)limits.maxTexelOffset;
